## 1 · Build
```bash
rosdep install --from-paths src -y --ignore-src
colcon build --symlink-install && source install/setup.bash
```

## 2 · Simulate, map and navigate (one command)
```bash
ros2 launch {{ pkg }} sim.launch.py
```
Gazebo Harmonic opens the TESR arena, RViz shows the map growing. Click **2D Goal Pose** in RViz — the robot plans
(Smac 2D), follows the path (MPPI, {{ p.mppi_motion_model }}) and keeps mapping. Save the map:
```bash
ros2 run nav2_map_server map_saver_cli -f ~/{{ d.meta.name }}_map
ros2 launch {{ pkg }} sim.launch.py slam:=false map:=$HOME/{{ d.meta.name }}_map.yaml   # AMCL on the saved map
```
Drive by keyboard: `ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard --ros-args -p stamped:=true`

## 3 · Real robot
```bash
ros2 launch {{ pkg }} robot.launch.py hardware:=real nav:=true
```
Motor driver plugin: `{{ p.real_plugin or 'not in the registry yet — mock hardware is used' }}`. Start the sensor drivers
({{ r.hardware|map(attribute='driver_package')|select|unique|join(', ') or '—' }}) so they publish {{ p.scan_topics|join(', ') or 'no LiDAR' }}.

